   {
    "id": 50656056,
    "type": "comment",
    "by": "user2",
    "text": "Happy Thanksgiving HN!<p>Grateful for the people who have made little tools and big tools and charming little projects, and insightful posts, and anything in between. Tech opens new opportunities like maps in broad dark space and the tinkerers light the way and show what\u2019s newly possible.<p>Also grateful to the gadgets and environments and people around tinkerers who take care of the meat-space parts to free up more time for research and insights.<p>The world is full of distractions and it takes a special kind of person to ignore those and dig down into obscure API or fight through the last 20% to take a project to production. The latest numbers I read show AI has helped people who already publish to publish more, but I think those works may inspire more people to make new things as well.<p>Here is a little game I made with the kids to be played with friends and family in person around the holidays. <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;santawho.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;santawho.com</a> Cheers to more giggles and less social media doom and gloom!",
    "time": 1795705324,
    "createdAt": "2026-11-26T15:02:04.000Z",
    "parent": 50655664,
    "depth": 1,
    "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50656056"
   },
